    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d734">

                <pb facs="0850" n="1684" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1684"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/933</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Willard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-04T19:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 4, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1197. For Chadbourne [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 90. Your 81, Embassy’s 1366, May 28, 10 a.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d734-f1"/>
                    Smith will arrive Madrid about June 20 to take up shipping negotiation. He
                    advises and you may announce, if you approve, an extension of our arrangement of
                    March 7<anchor n="2" xml:id="d734-f2"/> respecting bunker regulations to and
                    including June 25. Cailler representing Swiss Government is proceeding to Madrid
                    to negotiate for enemy boats in Spain.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
